 "constraints": [],
 "stem": "Find the value of ${=a}\\sin 30^\\circ+{=b}\\cos 60^\\circ+{=c}\\tan 45^\\circ$.",
 "answer": "a // 2 + b // 2 + c",
 "solution": [
  "In the equilateral triangle ABC of side 2L with AD perpendicular to BC, BD = L, AB = 2L, and m(∠BAD) = 30°, m(∠B) = 60°.",
  "So $\\sin 30^\\circ=\\frac{BD}{AB}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\cos 60^\\circ=\\frac{BD}{AB}=\\frac{1}{2}$.",
  "In the isosceles right-angled triangle with legs L, the angles are 45°, so $\\tan 45^\\circ=\\frac{L}{L}=1$.",
  "${=a}\\times\\frac{1}{2}={=a // 2}$ and ${=b}\\times\\frac{1}{2}={=b // 2}$ and ${=c}\\times 1={=c}$.",
  "The value is ${=a // 2}+{=b // 2}+{=c}={=a // 2 + b // 2 + c}$."
 ],
 "proposed_misconceptions": [],
 "notes": "Uses sin30=cos60=1/2 and tan45=1 as derived in the book triangles. a and b even so the answer is whole."
